| Crate | Category | Colour |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Printed circuit boards | Green |
| 2 | Batteries — hazardous | Red |
| 3 | Copper coils, transformers, motors | Orange |
| 4 | Cables and wires | Yellow |
| 5 | Display panels | Blue |
| 6 | Glass and engineered plastics | Purple |
| — | Unknown / Needs Review | Grey |

The same colour must be used consistently in:
- Scan result screens
- Crate inventory cards
- Sorting instructions
- Crate labels
- Recycler listings
- Reports

Do not rely on colour alone. Always pair colours with icons, text labels, and spoken instructions so that users with colour-vision deficiencies can still use the application.

The red battery crate is a category identifier, not a claim that ordinary storage in a crate makes batteries safe. Actual storage and handling must follow suitable safety requirements.

The Unknown crate is a logical review state. Do not assume that all uncertain or hazardous materials should be physically placed together in one container. Actual storage must follow material-specific safety guidance.

